// Argus remediation: histogram-bucket-mismatch — MET-001 on "checkout"
// Metric: http_requests_total
// Generated by `argus remediate` — review before applying.
//
// HONEST NOTE: a collector cannot re-bucket a histogram. Buckets are chosen by
// the SDK that records it, and quantiles computed across series with
// different (or missing) bucket bounds are wrong. The fix is in the
// application:
//   1. Give the histogram explicit bucket boundaries with an SDK View, the same
//      boundaries in every service and every replica that records it.
//   2. Or switch it to an exponential (base-2) histogram, which needs no
//      boundaries and merges across differing scales, if your backend accepts
//      native histograms.
//   3. Roll the change out to every instance before comparing quantiles:
//      during the rollout both layouts coexist.
//
// There is no collector configuration to generate for this finding.
